# Findings gitleaks must not re-report. One fingerprint per line, as
# gitleaks prints it: <commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>.
#
# Scoped to a SINGLE finding in a SINGLE historical commit -- not a path
# or a rule -- so everything else in that file, and every future commit
# touching it, is still scanned in full.
#
# Why this is here: the nightly `schedule:` run checks out with
# fetch-depth 0 and scans the WHOLE history, so a finding in an already
# pushed commit keeps secret-scan red forever even after the working
# tree is fixed. The literal below is a test constant for
# Homelab::Common::SetupToken's unit tests; it was flagged on entropy
# alone, and the current tree no longer contains it (common/t/setuptoken.t
# assembles the value at runtime instead). This line retires the
# historical hit only.
